00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:04.870 align:start position:0%
rmx logic data science is a program  focused on data science for biomedical  data  as seen in application to project source  from current topics  in biomedical research in this program  we will focus on methods of data  analysis  and data wrangling essential skills for  bioinformaticians  as well as those interested in other  types of non-biology related research  using data analysis we will take a  variety of research examples and learn  about the logic behind each type of  omics data  used to study cancer tissue biology and  the microbiome  we will speak about data processing a  procedure  to generate a data set or a matrix of  continuous and categorical data  from a biological sample that can be  then visualized  and analyzed in a statistical way to do  so  you will be able to run complex  bioinformatics pipelines  on high performance computing and  cloud-based servers  without slowing down your own computer  and develop  a logical understanding of many methods  involved  in the data preparation steps these are  commonly used  to study dna variation gene expression  protein abundance and composition  properties of microbial communities  these are all very different types of  data that we will learn to explore  and mine for patterns we will learn to  plot histograms  scatter plots and bar plots to find  relationships between data  and explore ways to categorize millions  of data points per sample  then we will use these visual  representations to spot technical noise  that is important to eliminate using  various normalization techniques  and data transformation steps in  practical coding assignments  we will also help you understand the r  and python code  elements that will be a part of any data  science project you end up working on  in your future these exercises are  designed  to explain the code and help you adapt  it to a project of your own  with clean and efficient code practices  we will also have a chance to see how  data could be mined for patterns  and machine learning is used to group  data objects by feature similarity  and models are trained for predictive  analysis  these help simplify data for  visualization  that can then be used for spotting  relationships and patterns  in complex data sets in week one  we will focus on our mix data types  challenges associated with big data  and give you an overview of different  methods to handle and prepare data for  in-depth analysis in week two of the  program  we will focus on multivariate analysis  methods  and examples using machine learning and  artificial intelligence  we welcome you to join the armix logic  data science program  it is a training experience on data  science approaches for biomedical data  as seen in application to project source  from current topics  in biomedical research
 

